{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added a nullable `word_count` column to `entries` (new migration; existing rows are left NULL, not backfilled). The word count is computed in the storage layer on every entry save \u2014 create, feed-refresh update, and title/content update \u2014 as the number of whitespace-separated words in the content after `sanitizer.StripTags`. It is exposed as `word_count` (`*int`, null where unknown) on `model.Entry` and the Go client `Entry`, and read back through the entry query builder.\n\nBuild, unit tests (53 packages) and integration tests (102) pass; no new tests were added for the word count itself.\n\nOne behaviour to be aware of: tags are removed without inserting whitespace, so `<p>a</p><p>b</p>` counts as one word. This matches how the existing reading-time estimate strips tags.", "t": 1794461780.421}
